{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1252788-court-goodwill-and-mantle-specific-merits","id":1252788,"title":"Court Goodwill, and Mantle specific merits","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-09-09T10:01:51-07:00","id":1252788,"title":"Court Goodwill, and Mantle specific merits","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> <br /> I was wondering, can Court Goodwill replace Mantle as a prerequisite? I mean for merits like Firebrand, Grounded, Cloak of Leaves, Cold Hearted?<br /> <br /> Thanks,<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-09T11:01:20-07:00","id":1252806,"title":"","content":"Nah.<br /> <br /> Storytellers can do as they like at their table, of course, and nothing will really break. They're not unbalancing. But the Mantle-specific Merits aren't anything a character really needs or loses out on a concept without, and keeping them proprietary helps add a little more mechanical backing to distinguishing the Courts and their courtiers.<br /> <br /> They're also at relatively high Mantle ratings when you factor in that an equal rating of Court Goodwill probably shouldn't yield quite as much as actual membership in the Court should. They require the same Mantle rating that you need to learn Royal Court Contracts, which require a whopping five dots of Court Goodwill, suggesting where you might tag the prerequisite if you do allow it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"